exit 0
--- stdout
oikade deploy: Check and build your home, and run it on the host.

The host keeps the version it was running until the new one has stayed up, and
puts it back if it doesn't. A deploy that would end a Safety rule's claims needs
--allow-safety-removal.

[1mUsage:[0m
  oikade deploy [--module DIR | --binary FILE] [--allow-safety-removal]

[1mFlags:[0m
  --module DIR            Your home's module, to check and build. (default .)
  --binary FILE           A binary already built for the host, skipping the
                          source checks.
  --allow-safety-removal  Go ahead even though a Safety rule would go.
  --context NAME          The host to reach over its network API, from oikade
                          login.
  --data-dir DIR          The host's data directory, on this machine. (default
                          /var/lib/oikade)

[1mExample:[0m
  oikade deploy --module ~/my-home
--- stderr
